BOARD — CUSTOM COLUMN SUPPORT (backend fix needed)
=====================================================

PROBLEM
-------
Frontend lets a user add a custom column (e.g. "Review", "QA") via
SAVE_BOARD_STATUS. That only saves the column NAME in a separate lookup
table. When a card is moved into that custom column (via UPDATE_BOARD_STATUS
/ editBoard, setting status = "review"), the write succeeds, but the card
then disappears from GET_BOARD's response entirely. Confirmed live multiple
times: getBoard only ever returns cards whose status is exactly one of these
5 hardcoded values:

    in_discussion, to_do, in_work, in_progress, completed

Any other status value = card excluded from the response (not deleted in DB,
just not returned). So custom columns can be created but never actually hold
visible cards.


ENDPOINTS INVOLVED (current, already live)
-------------------------------------------

1. GET_BOARD                 POST /projectManager/getBoard
   *** THIS is the one that needs the fix. ***
   Request:
     { "project_id": 12 }
   Response (today — only 5 fixed buckets, custom statuses missing):
     {
       "success": true,
       "data": [
         { "id": 101, "project_id": 12, "task_id": 55, "resource_id": 4,
           "status": "to_do", "pm_id": 19 }
       ]
     }
   NEEDED: same response shape, but "status" should be allowed to be ANY
   value that exists in the statuses table (see SAVE_BOARD_STATUS below),
   not just the 5 hardcoded ones.

2. UPDATE_BOARD_STATUS        POST /users/editBoard   (aka UPDATE_BOARD)
   [NO CHANGE NEEDED — already works correctly]
   Request (FULL record required every call — partial body nulls out
   omitted fields):
     {
       "id": 101,
       "project_id": 12,
       "task_id": 55,
       "resource_id": 4,
       "status": "review",
       "pm_id": 19
     }
   Response:
     { "success": true, "message": "Board updated" }
   Already accepts any string in "status" without error — writes fine, the
   problem is only that getBoard (#1) won't return it afterward.

3. CREATE_BOARD               POST /users/create_board
   [NO CHANGE NEEDED — already works correctly]
   Request:
     {
       "project_id": 12,
       "task_id": 55,
       "resource_id": 4,
       "status": "to_do",
       "pm_id": 19
     }
   Response:
     { "success": true, "message": "Board created" }
   (Doesn't return the new row's id — caller must re-call getBoard to get it.)

4. SAVE_BOARD_STATUS          POST /projectManager/saveBoardStatus
   [NO CHANGE NEEDED — already works correctly]
   Request:
     { "status": "Review" }
   Response:
     { "success": true, "data": { "id": 6, "status": "Review" } }
   Only registers a column NAME in a separate table — unrelated to getBoard.

5. GET_BOARD_STATUS           GET  /projectManager/getBoardStatus
   [NO CHANGE NEEDED — already works correctly]
   Request: none (no body/params)
   Response:
     {
       "success": true,
       "count": 6,
       "data": [
         { "id": 1, "status": "in_discussion", "created_at": "2026-01-01" },
         { "id": 6, "status": "Review", "created_at": "2026-08-20" }
       ]
     }

6. RENAME_BOARD_STATUS        POST /projectManager/editBoardStatus
   [NO CHANGE NEEDED — already works correctly]
   Request:
     { "id": 6, "status": "QA Review" }
   Response:
     { "success": true, "data": { "id": 6, "status": "QA Review" } }

7. DELETE_BOARD_STATUS        POST /projectManager/deleteBoardStatus
   [NO CHANGE NEEDED — already works correctly]
   Request:
     { "id": 6 }
   Response:
     { "success": true, "message": "Status deleted" }


WHAT NEEDS TO CHANGE (backend)
-------------------------------
GET_BOARD (getBoard) must stop hardcoding the 5 statuses. It should return
whatever status value is actually stored on each board row — dynamically,
not filtered to a fixed list. Ideally getBoard's grouping should be driven
off the same statuses table that saveBoardStatus/getBoardStatus writes to,
so any column a user creates is automatically a valid bucket getBoard can
return cards under.

No new endpoint is required — this is a fix to existing getBoard logic, not
a new API.


HOW THE 7 ENDPOINTS CONNECT TO EACH OTHER
------------------------------------------
saveBoardStatus  --writes--> statuses table  <--reads-- getBoardStatus
                                                 (used to populate column list)

editBoard (status field) --writes--> board_cards.status
getBoard  --reads--> board_cards, but filters to 5 fixed values (THE BUG)

editBoardStatus / deleteBoardStatus --only affect statuses table--
   (renaming/deleting a column name has ZERO effect on getBoard's card
   filtering today — confirmed live)

So today: column NAMES (statuses table) and column DATA (board_cards.status
filter in getBoard) are two disconnected systems. Fix = make getBoard read
from the same set of valid statuses instead of a fixed 5.
